P18-V01 Remoting request-context slice (2026-10-16)

- Compared the pinned Java 5.5.1 source at
  `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`. `NettyRequestProcessor.processRequest`
  and `RequestPipeline.execute` both receive `ChannelHandlerContext`; Rust inbound
  processing previously exposed only the peer address to processors and no
  context to pipeline stages.
- Added Rust-native `RequestContext` over the same identity-preserving
  `ChannelHandle` for pipeline and processor calls. It exposes channel identity,
  peer address, close, and immediate no-deadline `write_and_flush` enqueue with
  a future for the local write result. Existing `process_with_context` processors
  and pipeline implementations continue through default adapters.
- Added a loopback regression proving both piped stages and the processor receive
  the same channel handle, a context write reaches the peer, and the processor's
  ordinary response still completes. Added a unit regression for the legacy
  address-only processor adapter.
- Validation passed: `cargo test --workspace --locked`,
  `cargo test --workspace --all-features --locked`,
  `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked -- -D warnings`,
  `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, and `git diff --check`.
- Strict workspace Clippy initially reported `items-after-test-module` for an
  existing protocol-code import left below the new test module. Moved the import
  to the file header and reran strict Clippy successfully.
- Code/test commit: `eadcdb55` (`feat(remoting): pass request channel context`).
  Compatibility docs and release-checklist follow-up are in the separate docs
  commit for this slice.
- Java reference checkout remained read-only. No plan files, Docker profiles,
  live Broker, or production environment were modified or used.
- This closes only the request-context capability slice. The remaining Netty
  handler-context surface and broad bidirectional P18-V01 source/API/input/error/
  control-flow/reverse-export audit remain open; no full Phase 18 acceptance is
  claimed.
